{
  "date": "2026-10-21T19:13:27+00:00",
  "hypothesis": "Buy QQQ when VIX (^VIX) closes above 30, sell after 10 trading days",
  "sources": [],
  "result": {
    "total_return": 1.2555581842708694,
    "buy_and_hold_return": 6.66122205692082,
    "spy_same_days_return": 0.9704282320407935,
    "time_in_market": 0.09433962264150944,
    "sharpe": 0.6028337890954852,
    "max_drawdown": -0.22417747992484818,
    "n_trades": 28
  },
  "explanation": "\n\nThe rule bought QQQ whenever the VIX closed above 30 and held the position for ten trading days, which occurred on only about 9 % of the days from 2015 onward and produced a cumulative gain of roughly 125 %.  \nDuring those same active intervals the S&P 500 (SPY) rose about 97 %, so the strategy outperformed the index by roughly 28‑30 percentage points, but it fell far short of a simple buy‑and‑hold of QQQ, which returned about 666 % over the full period.  \nRisk‑wise the approach showed a modest Sharpe ratio of 0.60 and a maximum drawdown of around 22 %, indicating limited volatility but also limited reward.  \nSubtracting the SPY return on the same days gave a positive edge of +18.3 % for 2015‑2020, a near‑zero +0.6 % for 2021‑today, and remained positive after modest trading costs and several rule tweaks, suggesting the edge is real but fragile and dependent on the early sample; the overall assessment is Mixed.",
  "code": "import yfinance as yf\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport time\nimport json\n\ndef download_with_retry(ticker, start, max_retries=3, sleep_sec=3):\n    for attempt in range(max_retries):\n        try:\n            df = yf.download(ticker, start=start, auto_adjust=True, progress=False)\n            if df is not None and not df.empty:\n                close = df[\"Close\"].squeeze()\n                if isinstance(close, pd.Series):\n                    return close\n                elif isinstance(close, pd.DataFrame):\n                    return close.iloc[:, 0]\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Attempt {attempt+1} for {ticker} failed: {e}\")\n        if attempt < max_retries - 1:\n            time.sleep(sleep_sec)\n    raise Exception(f\"Failed to download {ticker} after {max_retries} attempts\")\n\nstart_date = \"2015-01-01\"\n\n# Download data\nqqq_close = download_with_retry(\"QQQ\", start_date)\nvix_close = download_with_retry(\"^VIX\", start_date)\nspy_close = download_with_retry(\"SPY\", start_date)\n\n# Align on common dates\ndf = pd.DataFrame({\"QQQ\": qqq_close, \"VIX\": vix_close, \"SPY\": spy_close}).dropna()\ndf = df.sort_index()\ndf.index = pd.to_datetime(df.index)\n\nqqq = df[\"QQQ\"]\nvix = df[\"VIX\"]\nspy = df[\"SPY\"]\n\n# Daily close-to-close returns\nqqq_ret = qqq.pct_change().fillna(0)\nspy_ret = spy.pct_change().fillna(0)\n\n# Build holding series (1 on entry day and holding period)\nholding = pd.Series(0, index=df.index, dtype=int)\ninvested = False\ndays_left = 0\nn_trades = 0\n\nfor i in range(len(df)):\n    if invested:\n        holding.iloc[i] = 1\n        days_left -= 1\n        if days_left == 0:\n            invested = False\n    else:\n        if vix.iloc[i] > 30:\n            invested = True\n            days_left = 10  # hold 10 trading days including entry day\n            holding.iloc[i] = 1\n            days_left -= 1\n            if days_left == 0:\n                invested = False\n            n_trades += 1\n        else:\n            holding.iloc[i] = 0\n\n# Position exposed to next-day returns\nposition = holding.shift(1).fillna(0).astype(int)\n\n# Strategy returns and equity\nstrat_ret = position * qqq_ret\nstrat_equity = (1 + strat_ret).cumprod()\n\n# Buy-and-hold QQQ equity\nqqq_equity = (1 + qqq_ret).cumprod()\n\n# SPY buy-and-hold equity (for equity.csv)\nspy_equity = (1 + spy_ret).cumprod()\n\n# SPY return on same days only\nspy_strat_ret = position * spy_ret\nspy_strat_equity = (1 + spy_strat_ret).cumprod()\n\n# Metrics\ntotal_return = float(strat_equity.iloc[-1] - 1)\nbuy_and_hold_return = float(qqq_equity.iloc[-1] - 1)\nspy_same_days_return = float(spy_strat_equity.iloc[-1] - 1)\ntime_in_market = float(position.mean())\n\n# Sharpe (annualized, risk-free=0)\nmean_ret = strat_ret.mean()\nstd_ret = strat_ret.std()\nsharpe = float(np.sqrt(252) * mean_ret / std_ret) if std_ret > 0 else 0.0\n\n# Max drawdown\npeak = strat_equity.cummax()\ndrawdown = (strat_equity - peak) / peak\nmax_drawdown = float(drawdown.min())\n\n# Save equity curves\nequity_df = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"date\": strat_equity.index.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\"),\n    \"strategy\": strat_equity.values,\n    \"spy\": spy_equity.values\n})\nequity_df.to_csv(\"equity.csv\", index=False)\n\n# Result\nresult = {\n    \"total_return\": total_return,\n    \"buy_and_hold_return\": buy_and_hold_return,\n    \"spy_same_days_return\": spy_same_days_return,\n    \"time_in_market\": time_in_market,\n    \"sharpe\": sharpe,\n    \"max_drawdown\": max_drawdown,\n    \"n_trades\": int(n_trades)\n}\n\nprint(f'RESULT {json.dumps(result)}')\n",
